  "accounting": "Adopted 2026–2027 TER Articles 7.1, 10.2, 11.3 and the year-two curriculum table establish the general English full-time degree. Year one has ten 6 EC units and a non-credit test. Year two has seven 6 EC required units plus History of Science at 3 EC and three independent constrained selections in periods 3, 5 and 6. Year three has 30 EC prescribed, including the 15 EC Bachelor Project, and 30 open. The official annual Algorithms II and security module entries corroborate the TER, which controls over the overview repeat of Algorithms I. Current Smart Systems replaces Pervasive Computing.",
  "progression": "The adopted regulations define an English full-time general degree with no formal specialization. Year one has 60 EC required. Year two combines 45 EC required with separate 3, 6 and 6 EC constrained choices in periods 3, 5 and 6. This example uses Academic Writing, Introduction to Computer Security and Human-Computer Interaction respectively. Algorithms II, not the repeated Algorithms I wording on the programme overview, is required. Year three has 30 EC of open study and 30 EC required, including the 15 EC Bachelor Project. The English test and any required refresher carry no extra credits. Article 9.1 requires prior Computer Programming or Systems Programming Project for Object-Oriented and Functional Programming and Operating Systems. A specified earlier two-course programming sequence also qualifies for the former. Project admission requires 120 EC from the Computer Science bachelor. Project work may be individual or in a group. Two examiners assess technical work, thesis and presentation individually, weighted 50%, 40% and 10%, with at least 5.5 in each.",
